   116	
   117	D442's procedure (`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md`, "Procedure", steps 3 to 6) is run as it was run then, on both
   118	systems' draws as they stood at 07-14. It compares the answers the systems actually gave; MATCHING-v2 §4's adapter, which would re-ask
   119	the ruler's question, is not built (D442's precedent).
   120	- **The as-of state:** every view created on or before 2026-07-14 is listed first: by `created_seq` up to the last sequence of 07-14,
   121	  closed views included. Then `service.state_as_of` at 2026-07-14 is read for each one. New-system units are joined by
   122	  `clean_ladders.view_id`, split children included.
   123	- **Step 4, matching:** MATCHING-v2's SAME rule, two blind families and a third reader on each disagreement, with D442's rule for a ruler
   124	  question's candidates.
   125	- **Step 5, eligibility:** question, period and quantity the ruler's, and due day the ruler's (D430). Decided by two blind readers with
   126	  a third on disagreement; the literal reading (the same due day) beside.
   127	- **Step 6, outcomes:** the first that applies, (i) to (ix).
   128	  - Several SAME views: the first created is judged and the others listed.
   129	  - A figure rung with no bound: "no comparison".
   130	  - Agreement by the frozen scorer's rule (`prod_records.outcome` for the old system; for the new system the same rule, as Stage B counted
   131	    it: "Ruled out" and "Still open" answer no, `stage_b/control_theses.py`).
   132	- **Printed:** per ruler question and draw, its outcome; and per draw and system, the agreements on the seven graded questions.
   133	
   134	## 4. The floors (printed beside; proposed, not gates)
   135	
   136	As their source states them (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-10/codex-1.md`; `RUN-PLAN-v2.md` §1.6). Each floor is
   137	computed per draw and under both countings, and holds when it is met in at least 2 of the system's 3 draws:
   138	- **Covered:** at least 80% of important matters have a covering question.
   139	- **Trivial or duplicate:** at most 20% of the questions, counted as decided worth marks on every random-sample card, covering cards
   140	  included. The frozen rule keeps covering cards out of the guardrail shares only.
   141	- **Supported:** at least 90% of latest answers, counted on every answered random-sample card. An insufficient or unresolved answer is
   142	  counted and gets no credit.
   143	
   144	Wrong citations and answer-changing omissions: **not measured**.
   145	
   146	## Tables
   147	
   148	**Value × reader:**
   149	
   150	| Value | Written by | Read by |
   151	|---|---|---|
   152	| `eligibility.json` (all fingerprints) | eligibility | every §1.6 tool, export, scorer |
   153	| d400 code check | `d400_code_check` | report: release status |
   154	| d400 reader lines 1–5 | `d400_reader_lines.py` (Stage A's tools on verified copies) | report: printed beside only |
   155	| step2-lines.json | `step2_lines.py` | report: release status |
   156	| d431-0714.json | `d431_reading.py` | report |
   157	| beside quantities | `score_comparison.beside` | report |
   158	
   159	**State × event:**
   160	
   161	| Event | Handling |
   162	|---|---|
   163	| A reader session voids | Retried once, then reported missing. A line with a missing mark is not measured |
   164	| A draw stopped or ineligible | No release verdict. `eligibility.py` still records every finished draw's fingerprints and names the draws that stop the aggregate. The tools run on what finished, as a diagnostic (plan §1.4 item 10) |
   165	| A file changed after eligibility | The tool refuses |
   166	| A component was redone | Its counted folder is the one `run.json` names |
  9800	    - The floors follow their source: per draw, met in at least 2 of 3, and an insufficient answer counted without credit.
  9801	    - D400 line 5 is scaled per D452.
  9802	    - The days to opening name an opening before the first listed article, apart from the warm-up.
  9803	  - **A reading recorded before any output** (both readers agreed in round 6): a hard check that is not measured cannot clear
